  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of life-sustaining and life-saving interventions to the conflict-affected population with a special focus on the women, adolescent girls and children in Cabo Delgado province north of Mozambique.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This WHO health project aims to reduce morbidity and mortality for internally displaced people, returnees, and people from the host communities. WHO provides primary health care services through temporary clinics (mobile brigades), Mental Health and Psychosocial Support (MHPSS) services, and supports the provision of safe blood transfusion services in the health facilities where Comprehensive Emergency Obstetric and Newborn Care is provided. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 92,000 people, including 21,160 women, 19,320 men, 51,520  children, and including 4600 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
